rain-core: xray/0052-muxcool-xray-modes
Source: ReClash fix on top of xray/0037 (GPL-3.0).

Xray spells the mux options concurrency, xudpConcurrency and
xudpProxyUDP443, and concurrency: 0 means "no TCP pool" rather than "use the
default". Accept those aliases without changing the historical kebab keys:
an explicit alias wins, an absent one leaves max-concurrency: 0 at its old
meaning. A TCP-disabled block with an XUDP pool is Xray's UDP-only mux, which
is also the one Vision combination Xray allows (the server restricts a Vision
Mux carrier to UDP); TCP then goes over plain VLESS with Vision and only UDP
is multiplexed. A block with no pool left is ignored with a warning.

Tests: parser alias/TCP-disabled/Vision tests, outbound TCP-disabled and
no-pool tests.
